    "physical_description": "Carpet:\r\n\r\nWARP: cream wool; Z2S; 16 threads per inch (64 per dm).\r\n\r\nWEFT: brown and cream wool, usually plied together; Z2S; 2 shoots after each row of knots; 14 threads per inch (60 per dm).\r\n\r\nPILE: wool; 8 colours: red, light red, yellow, green, blue, dark pink, dark brown, white; symmetrical knot tied around two threads; 112 per sq. inch (1920 per sq. dm).\r\n\r\nSIDE FINISH: missing; a dark pink cord has been stitched in place to stabilise the edges.\r\n\r\nEND FINISH: cut\r\n\r\nDESIGN: Field: dark pink ground with 14 and two half bands of either 2 or 1 and two half hooked and quartered lozenges.  These form 3 and two half rows.  The central and two half rows have within them hooked diagonal lines.  The two other rows have within them stylised floral sprigs.\r\n\r\nMain border: light yellow ground; the sides have an angular dark pink meander with dark pink, blue or green curled leaves.  The lower border has V-shaped stylised flowers in place of leaves; the upper border has hooked diamonds in place of leaves.\r\n\r\nInner and outer (incomplete) borders: reciprocal horned triangles in red, green and blue with florets at the point.  Lower elem: dark pink ground with one band of stylised floral sprigs below a band of small triangles with pendants.\r\n\r\nUpper elem: incomplete with max of 12 cms. with one band of 6 spiked lozenges, each containing 9 small lozenges, apparently the lower part of a larger motif.  In the extreme top left there is part of a sprig.\r\n\r\nDate catalogued: 16.4.96",
